<title>GERMANY: Buba's Kuehbacher says no Italy in EMU from start.</title>
<headline>Buba's Kuehbacher says no Italy in EMU from start.</headline>
<dateline>POTSDAM, Germany 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy should not take part in European currency union from the beginning, Bundesbank council member Klaus-Dieter Kuehbacher, said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The Italians want to get in, but they shouldn't get in,&quot; Kuehbacher, also president of the Berlin-Brandenburg state central bank, said at a meeting of the German social democratic party, the SPD.</p>
<p>Kuehbacher said that Italy did not yet meet the fiscal requirements for monetary union, adding that he thought that Greece would also not be taking part from the start.</p>
</text>
